            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tmmiller26"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this with 7 chicken breasts. Doubled the ingredients. Added 1/2 teaspoon of garlic and dijon mustard to the mayo/cheese, and used panko bread crumbs instead of Italian. Baked for 30 minutes instead of 20, and it came out great! Served with cheesy mashed potatoes and garlic green beans.",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-28T23:39:23.185Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "pamjlee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Although I made some changes, I am rating this more for myself. I used miracle whip, personal preference. Also mixed in some garlic powder, pepper and dried basil. I then rolled the chicken pieces in the parmesan cheese. I left out the bread crumbs altogether. I had sliced the chicken breast into 4 pieces to have more coating so the cooking time was good for me. Very nice flavor, quick and easy. A keeper.",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-07T03:02:25.547Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RedChip8401"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My wife loves it....I pounded the chicken fillets. I did salt and pepper the chicken before coating with the mayo and cheese mixture, and Italian bread crumbs... I placed them on a grate on a cookie sheet...They were very good,",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-25T22:14:27.012Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’m generally very impressed with Hellmann’s recipes, but this time not so much. So I changed it up big time I guess. I salted and peppered the chicken breasts, then spread them with mayonnaise to which I added fresh minced garlic. I mixed panko bread crumbs and the grated Parmesan in a ratio of 2:1, and added fresh oregano, parsley and rosemary, topping each of the chicken breasts as the recipe directs. I gave them a drizzle of olive oil before popping them in the oven. I much preferred that method and those fresh ingredients rather than mixing the cheese in with the mayonnaise and using Italian seasoned bread crumbs which I don’t think I would have cared for. I sliced the chicken and served it over “Spinach Ranch Salad,” also from this site, and “Broccoli Cheese Soup V.”",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-01T12:01:40.643Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Danette Lykins"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful! I added more seasonings to the Mayo mix: seasoning salt, garlic powder, dash of cayenne and some lemon pepper.. coated chicken in mayo mix, and tossed them in a ziplock with bread crumbs. Sprinkle some paprika on top for a fancier look.. baked on rack over cookie sheet so the bottoms didn't get soggy- there are none for leftovers! will be making this again.",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-13T18:19:17.963Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cJoY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe &amp; it turned out GREAT, it was tasty, easy &amp; fast to make. Even though the recipe doesn't call for it, be sure to season your raw chicken breast before you add the mayo mixture &amp; bread crumbs or it may taste a bit bland. I seasoned my chicken w/Lawry's, garlic powder, black pepper &amp; a little thyme. I also cooked it for 30 mins, instead of 20 as the recipe states, doing that made the crust crispier &amp; less mushy.",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-08T20:32:52.590Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "VividSoy2109"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe that calls for only 4 ingredients! I’ve made this recipe twice. The first time I used plain breadcrumbs and added Italian Seasoning. The second time I used Panko and added Italian Seasoning. Rave reviews on both, but I think Panko makes a crispier crust. D-lish … Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-03T04:25:34.114Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elaine"
            },
            "reviewBody": "There is no better way to prepare chicken. I suggest pounding the pieces to get them even and adding about a tsp of mustard to the mayo---or a squeeze of lemon. Absolutely salt &amp; pepper and spice the chicken on both sides. A little cooking spray on top helps the breadcrumbs brown nicely.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-16T19:32:32.240Z"
          },
          {
